  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), which is a weak baseline. The single most important unresolved question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal. Question tested: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly compares image-only performance against the RNA-only baseline while holding profile_setting constant, isolating the modality effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It establishes the value of the image modality before investing in multimodal fusion configurations, which would otherwise conflate modality contribution with fusion mechanics. (2) The result will strongly guide all downstream choices—if image is competitive with RNA, multimodal fusion (configs 016–051) becomes high-priority; if image is weak, effort should shift to RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. (3) resnet50 is a standard, well-calibrated encoder that gives a clean read on whether image features are informative at all, without the added complexity of a very large ViT. (4) Under a tight budget, this single experiment reduces the most critical uncertainty and maximally informs the structure of the remaining search space."
}

